{"step_index":3488,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T18:31:58Z","thinking":"Processing ambiguous cases now involves LLM integration if applicable. The original batching method is simplified and conditionally applied based on configuration existence. This indicates a potential optimization or alternative execution path is being implemented for handling ambiguous cases.\n\n\nAmbiguous items are being sent to a local API in batches, with retries implemented to handle potential transient issues. The results are parsed to determine match status, item IDs, and reasons for each case.  A check is in place to ensure a warehouse item exists for \"match\" or \"review\" statuses, falling back to \"no_match\" if missing and no candidates are available.\n\n\nThe processing loop aggregates match/review counts for each batch, updating internal metrics.  An error handling mechanism is built-in; specifically, rate limiting and large payload failures trigger retries or chunk splitting.  The split logic aims to resolve failures by dividing large batches into smaller, more manageable sub-batches.\n\n\nIf an API call fails, the batch is divided and retried, potentially resolving issues related to payload size or temporary service instability. The initial attempt uses a larger batch; only upon failure is the batch split. The split is performed by sending the front and back half of the original cases chunk to the processing. The total number of retries is configurable.\n\n\nThe local API call utilizes a configurable model for processing the ambiguous input data. The API request is constructed with a system prompt and the input data, handling potential non-ASCII characters.  A hardcoded API key is used for authorization and the endpoint is configurable as well. If the API returns a non-200 status, a runtime error is raised.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Implement adaptive single-batching and splitting in FastCoordinator","EndLine":308,"Instruction":"Replace batch_size loop with adaptive single-batch and splitting logic","ReplacementContent":"        # 3. Process via LLM for the ambiguous ones\n        if llm_cases and hasattr(self.config, 'local_api_url'):\n            print(f\"  -> Sending {len(llm_cases)} ambiguous items to Local API (MSEMAX)...\")\n            \n            def send_batch_adaptive(cases_chunk, chunk_name=\"1\"):\n                max_retries = 3\n                for attempt in range(max_retries):\n                    try:\n                        print(f\"      [*] Sending batch {chunk_name} ({len(cases_chunk)} items) to LLM (Attempt {attempt+1}/{max_retries})...\")\n                        time.sleep(2)  # Polite pacing delay\n                        raw_results = self._call_local_api({\"cases\": cases_chunk})\n                        \n                        parsed = []\n                        matched_in_chunk = 0\n                        review_in_chunk = 0\n                        for case, decision in zip(cases_chunk, raw_results):\n                            shortage_name = case[\"requested_name\"]\n                            status = decision.get(\"status\", \"no_match\")\n                            item_id = decision.get(\"item_id\", \"\")\n                            warehouse_item = catalog_by_id.get(item_id, \"\")\n                            reason = decision.get(\"reason\", \"\")\n                            \n                            if status in (\"match\", \"review\") and not warehouse_item:\n                                if case.get(\"candidates\"):\n                                    warehouse_item = case[\"candidates\"][0][\"name\"]\n                                else:\n                                    status = \"no_match\"\n                                    \n                            if status == \"match\":\n                                matched_in_chunk += 1\n                            elif status == \"review\":\n                                review_in_chunk += 1\n                                \n                            parsed.append({\n                                \"shortage_name\": shortage_name,\n                                \"status\": status,\n                                \"warehouse_item\": warehouse_item,\n                                \"reason\": reason\n                            })\n                        print(f\"      [✓] Batch {chunk_name} ({len(cases_chunk)} items) finished: {matched_in_chunk} matched, {review_in_chunk} review.\")\n                        return parsed\n                    except Exception as e:\n                        err_str = str(e)\n                        # Handle 429 Rate limit\n                        if \"429\" in err_str:\n                            wait_sec = 20 * (attempt + 1)\n                            print(f\"      [!] HTTP 429 Rate Limit on batch {chunk_name}. Waiting {wait_sec}s before retry...\")\n                            time.sleep(wait_sec)\n                            continue\n                        \n                        # If error is due to payload / incomplete json / timeout and chunk can be split\n                        if len(cases_chunk) > 40:\n                            mid = len(cases_chunk) // 2\n                            print(f\"      [!] Batch {chunk_name} ({len(cases_chunk)} items) failed with error: {e}\")\n                            print(f\"      [*] Adaptively splitting into 2 sub-batches: ({mid} items) and ({len(cases_chunk) - mid} items)...\")\n                            time.sleep(2)\n                            sub1 = send_batch_adaptive(cases_chunk[:mid], f\"{chunk_name}.1\")\n                            time.sleep(2)\n                            sub2 = send_batch_adaptive(cases_chunk[mid:], f\"{chunk_name}.2\")\n                            return sub1 + sub2\n                        else:\n                            wait_sec = 5 * (attempt + 1)\n                            print(f\"      [!] Attempt {attempt+1} error ({e}). Waiting {wait_sec}s...\")\n                            time.sleep(wait_sec)\n                \n                print(f\"      [!] Batch {chunk_name} ({len(cases_chunk)} items) completely failed after {max_retries} attempts.\")\n                return [{\"shortage_name\": c[\"requested_name\"], \"status\": \"no_match\", \"warehouse_item\": \"\", \"reason\": \"\"} for c in cases_chunk]\n\n            # Start by sending all ambiguous items in 1 single message\n            results_list = send_batch_adaptive(llm_cases, \"1\")\n            \n            for result in results_list:\n                if result[\"status\"] == \"match\":\n                    matched.append({\n                        \"shortage_item\": result[\"shortage_name\"],\n                        \"warehouse_item\": result[\"warehouse_item\"],\n                        \"confidence\": \"llm\",\n                        \"method\": \"fast_llm\"\n                    })\n                elif result[\"status\"] == \"review\":\n                    needs_review.append({\n                        \"shortage_item\": result[\"shortage_name\"],\n                        \"warehouse_item\": result[\"warehouse_item\"],\n                        \"reason\": result.get(\"reason\", \"\")\n                    })\n\n        print(f\"  -> Final Warehouse Result: {len(matched)} matched, {len(needs_review)} review\")\n        return {\"matched\": matched, \"needs_review\": needs_review}\n\n    def _call_local_api(self, inputs: dict) -> list[dict]:\n        model = getattr(self.config, 'local_model', 'gpt-4o')\n        \n        body = {\n            \"model\": model,\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": SYSTEM_PROMPT},\n                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": json.dumps(inputs, ensure_ascii=False)}\n            ]\n        }\n\n        url = getattr(self.config, 'local_api_url', \"http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1/chat/completions\")\n        api_key = getattr(self.config, 'local_api_key', '[REDACTED_CREDENTIAL]')\n        \n        response = http_requests.post(\n            url,\n            headers={\n                \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {api_key}\",\n                \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n            },\n            json=body,\n            timeout=(30, 300),\n        )\n\n        if response.status_code != 200:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"HTTP {response.status_code}: {response.text[:200]}\")\n\n        resp_json = response.json()\n        content = resp_json[\"choices\"][0][\"message\"][\"content\"]\n        \n        # Clean markdown wrappers if any\n        clean = content.strip()\n        if \"```\" in clean:\n            clean = re.sub(r\"^```(?:json)?\\s*\", \"\", clean, flags=re.MULTILINE)\n            clean = re.sub(r\"```\\s*$\", \"\", clean, flags=re.MULTILINE)\n            clean = clean.strip()\n            \n        json_match = re.search(r'\\{.*\\}', clean, re.DOTALL)\n        if json_match:\n            clean = json_match.group(0)\n            \n        answer = json.loads(clean)\n        results = answer.get(\"results\", [])\n        \n        # Map by case_id\n        decision_map = {d.get(\"case_id\"): d for d in results}\n        \n        return [decision_map.get(c[\"case_id\"], {\"status\": \"no_match\", \"item_id\": \"\"}) for c in inputs[\"cases\"]]","StartLine":196,"TargetContent":"        # 3. Batch process via LLM for the ambiguous ones\n        if llm_cases and hasattr(self.config, 'local_api_url'):\n            print(f\"  -> Sending {len(llm_cases)} ambiguous items to Local API (MSEMAX) in batches...\")\n            batch_size = 30\n            batches = []\n            for i in range(0, len(llm_cases), batch_size):\n                batches.append((i//batch_size, llm_cases[i:i+batch_size]))\n                \n            def process_batch(batch_data):\n                batch_idx, batch_cases = batch_data\n                max_retries = 3\n                \n                # Pacing to respect wrapper's 10 req/min (1 req every 6 seconds on average)\n                time.sleep(6.5)\n                \n                for attempt in range(max_retries):\n                    try:\n                        results = self._call_local_api({\"cases\": batch_cases})\n                        parsed = []\n                        for case, decision in zip(batch_cases, results):\n                            shortage_name = case[\"requested_name\"]\n                            status = decision.get(\"status\", \"no_match\")\n                            item_id = decision.get(\"item_id\", \"\")\n                            warehouse_item = catalog_by_id.get(item_id, \"\")\n                            reason = decision.get(\"reason\", \"\")\n                            \n                            if status in (\"match\", \"review\") and not warehouse_item:\n                                if case.get(\"candidates\"):\n                                    warehouse_item = case[\"candidates\"][0][\"name\"]\n                                else:\n                                    status = \"no_match\"\n                                    \n                            parsed.append({\n                                \"shortage_name\": shortage_name,\n                                \"status\": status,\n                                \"warehouse_item\": warehouse_item,\n                                \"reason\": reason\n                            })\n                        print(f\"      [✓] Batch {batch_idx+1}/{len(batches)} done.\")\n                        return parsed\n                    except Exception as e:\n                        if attempt < max_retries - 1:\n                            wait_time = 5 * (attempt + 1)\n                            print(f\"      [!] Batch {batch_idx+1} error. Waiting {wait_time}s...\")\n                            time.sleep(wait_time)\n                        else:\n                            print(f\"      [!] Batch {batch_idx+1} completely failed: {e}\")\n                \n                return [{\"shortage_name\": c[\"requested_name\"], \"status\": \"no_match\", \"warehouse_item\": \"\", \"reason\": \"\"} for c in batch_cases]\n\n            # Wrapper says: \"Max concurrent: 3\". Using 2 to be extremely safe.\n            with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=2) as executor:\n                results_lists = list(executor.map(process_batch, batches))\n                \n            for res_list in results_lists:\n                for result in res_list:\n                    if result[\"status\"] == \"match\":\n                        matched.append({\n                            \"shortage_item\": result[\"shortage_name\"],\n                            \"warehouse_item\": result[\"warehouse_item\"],\n                            \"confidence\": \"llm\",\n                            \"method\": \"fast_llm\"\n                        })\n                    elif result[\"status\"] == \"review\":\n                        needs_review.append({\n                            \"shortage_item\": result[\"shortage_name\"],\n                            \"warehouse_item\": result[\"warehouse_item\"],\n                            \"reason\": result.get(\"reason\", \"\")\n                        })\n\n        print(f\"  -> Final Warehouse Result: {len(matched)} matched, {len(needs_review)} review\")\n        return {\"matched\": matched, \"needs_review\": needs_review}\n\n    def _call_local_api(self, inputs: dict) -> list[dict]:\n        model = getattr(self.config, 'local_model', 'gpt-4o')\n        \n        body = {\n            \"model\": model,\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": SYSTEM_PROMPT},\n                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": json.dumps(inputs, ensure_ascii=False)}\n            ]\n        }\n\n        url = getattr(self.config, 'local_api_url', \"http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1/chat/completions\")\n        api_key = getattr(self.config, 'local_api_key', '[REDACTED_CREDENTIAL]')\n        \n        response = http_requests.post(\n            url,\n            headers={\n                \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {api_key}\",\n                \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n            },\n            json=body,\n            timeout=(30, 300),\n        )\n\n        if response.status_code != 200:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"HTTP {response.status_code}\")\n\n        content = response.json()[\"choices\"][0][\"message\"][\"content\"]\n        json_match = re.search(r'\\{.*\\}', content, re.DOTALL)\n        if json_match:\n            content = json_match.group(0)\n            \n        answer = json.loads(content)\n        results = answer.get(\"results\", [])\n        \n        # Map by case_id\n        decision_map = {d.get(\"case_id\"): d for d in results}\n        \n        return [decision_map.get(c[\"case_id\"], {\"status\": \"no_match\", \"item_id\": \"\"}) for c in inputs[\"cases\"]]","TargetFile":"d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\src\\fast_match\\coordinator.py","toolAction":"Implement adaptive batching","toolSummary":"Replace batch loop with adaptive single-batch strategy"}}]}
