{"step_index":3526,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T18:42:29Z","thinking":"The \"Expecting value\" error triggered a chunk splitting mechanism. Due to a now-identified session expiration, each split sub-batch immediately failed with the same error. This cascade of failures then caused the chunk size to repeatedly halve. The root cause was not initially recognized as a session issue.\n\n\nThe local API call utilizes a specific model and constructs a request body with a system prompt and user input. It retrieves the URL and API key from the configuration; these are then used to make an HTTP POST request. If the response isn't successful, an exception is raised; otherwise, content is extracted, cleaned of specific error prefixes and markdown, and then parsed as JSON.\n\n\nThe JSON parse error suggests the model's output is malformed. The code maps returned decisions to their case IDs and handles missing cases. The user's instruction to send the entire input as one batch will be adopted. This could help test the model's ability to handle potentially large inputs.\n\n\nExamining the `send_batch` function, the code directly calls an internal API with the ambiguous items. A retry mechanism is implemented in case of failure. The results are then processed to update the matching status for each item based on the API response. There's a check to see if a matching item is already in the database.\n\n\nA retry mechanism is in place for API calls, incorporating exponential backoff for rate limiting errors. Session expiration errors are explicitly handled with a suggestion to refresh the session. Matched and review counts are tracked.\n\n\nThe code now processes results based on their status: \"match\" or \"review.\" Matched items are added to a \"matched\" list with confidence and method information. Items needing review are added to a \"needs_review\" list, along with a reason if available. The primary focus is on how to integrate the results within the code's data structures for accurate analysis.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Send all cases in 1 single message and detect MSEMAX session expired","EndLine":340,"Instruction":"Replace send_batch_adaptive with single message sending and clear session error handling","ReplacementContent":"        # 3. Process via LLM in 1 single message without splitting\n        if llm_cases and hasattr(self.config, 'local_api_url'):\n            print(f\"  -> Sending ALL {len(llm_cases)} ambiguous items to Local API (MSEMAX) in 1 SINGLE MESSAGE...\")\n            max_retries = 3\n            parsed_results = []\n            for attempt in range(max_retries):\n                try:\n                    time.sleep(2)\n                    raw_results = self._call_local_api({\"cases\": llm_cases})\n                    matched_count = 0\n                    review_count = 0\n                    for case, decision in zip(llm_cases, raw_results):\n                        shortage_name = case[\"requested_name\"]\n                        status = decision.get(\"status\", \"no_match\")\n                        item_id = decision.get(\"item_id\", \"\")\n                        warehouse_item = catalog_by_id.get(item_id, \"\")\n                        reason = decision.get(\"reason\", \"\")\n                        \n                        if status in (\"match\", \"review\") and not warehouse_item:\n                            if case.get(\"candidates\"):\n                                warehouse_item = case[\"candidates\"][0][\"name\"]\n                            else:\n                                status = \"no_match\"\n                                \n                        if status == \"match\":\n                            matched_count += 1\n                        elif status == \"review\":\n                            review_count += 1\n                            \n                        parsed_results.append({\n                            \"shortage_name\": shortage_name,\n                            \"status\": status,\n                            \"warehouse_item\": warehouse_item,\n                            \"reason\": reason\n                        })\n                    print(f\"      [✓] Single-message completed: {matched_count} matched, {review_count} review.\")\n                    break\n                except Exception as e:\n                    err_str = str(e)\n                    if \"session might be expired\" in err_str or \"Session expired\" in err_str:\n                        print(f\"      [!] خطأ في جلسة MSEMAX: انتهت صلاحية الجلسة على السيرفر.\")\n                        print(f\"      [!] يرجى تشغيل python get_session.py في مجلد MSEMAX لتحديث الجلسة.\")\n                        break\n                    if \"429\" in err_str:\n                        wait_sec = 25 * (attempt + 1)\n                        print(f\"      [!] HTTP 429 Rate Limit. Waiting {wait_sec}s before retry ({attempt+1}/{max_retries})...\")\n                        time.sleep(wait_sec)\n                    else:\n                        print(f\"      [!] Attempt {attempt+1}/{max_retries} error: {e}\")\n                        time.sleep(5)\n            \n            if not parsed_results:\n                parsed_results = [{\"shortage_name\": c[\"requested_name\"], \"status\": \"no_match\", \"warehouse_item\": \"\", \"reason\": \"\"} for c in llm_cases]\n\n            for result in parsed_results:\n                if result[\"status\"] == \"match\":\n                    matched.append({\n                        \"shortage_item\": result[\"shortage_name\"],\n                        \"warehouse_item\": result[\"warehouse_item\"],\n                        \"confidence\": \"llm\",\n                        \"method\": \"fast_llm\"\n                    })\n                elif result[\"status\"] == \"review\":\n                    needs_review.append({\n                        \"shortage_item\": result[\"shortage_name\"],\n                        \"warehouse_item\": result[\"warehouse_item\"],\n                        \"reason\": result.get(\"reason\", \"\")\n                    })\n\n        print(f\"  -> Final Warehouse Result: {len(matched)} matched, {len(needs_review)} review\")\n        return {\"matched\": matched, \"needs_review\": needs_review}\n\n    def _call_local_api(self, inputs: dict) -> list[dict]:\n        model = getattr(self.config, 'local_model', 'gpt-4o')\n        \n        body = {\n            \"model\": model,\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": SYSTEM_PROMPT},\n                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": json.dumps(inputs, ensure_ascii=False)}\n            ]\n        }\n\n        url = getattr(self.config, 'local_api_url', \"http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1/chat/completions\")\n        api_key = getattr(self.config, 'local_api_key', '[REDACTED_CREDENTIAL]')\n        \n        response = http_requests.post(\n            url,\n            headers={\n                \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {api_key}\",\n                \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n            },\n            json=body,\n            timeout=(30, 300),\n        )\n\n        if response.status_code != 200:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"HTTP {response.status_code}: {response.text[:200]}\")\n\n        resp_json = response.json()\n        content = resp_json[\"choices\"][0][\"message\"][\"content\"]\n        \n        # Check if MSEMAX returned an error string inside content\n        if content.strip().startswith(\"[Error:\"):\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"MSEMAX Error: {content.strip()}\")\n            \n        # Clean markdown wrappers if any\n        clean = content.strip()\n        if \"```\" in clean:\n            clean = re.sub(r\"^```(?:json)?\\s*\", \"\", clean, flags=re.MULTILINE)\n            clean = re.sub(r\"```\\s*$\", \"\", clean, flags=re.MULTILINE